                  <bindingDesc resp="#BCBB">
                     <binding notAfter="1625" notBefore="1575">
                        <p>16th century, late, or 17th century, <placeName key="place_1000095">Spanish</placeName>? (probably contemporary with manuscript): wood boards, slight inside bevel; 
                           dark brown leather, gilt tooled with roll and stamps to form on each cover a thin border with corner-pieces around a small centrepiece of ‘IH’S’ within an oval 
                           sunburst; gilding worn and rubbed, spine lost; remains of two fore-edge clasps with lost straps of similar leather (the surviving metalwork was probably 
                           originally under the leather); edges coloured red. Rebacked, late 19th or 20th century, Bodleian
                        </p>
